# Customize the SCM Report

By default, the SCM report uses the `<scm>` element of the POM, including one inherited from a parent.
To override these values, configure the `webAccessUrl`, `anonymousConnection` and `developerConnection`
parameters of the [scm goal](../scm-mojo.html).

This helps when the site is built from a module whose `<scm>` points to a subdirectory, and the
report should tell readers how to check out the whole repository:

```xml
<project>
  ...
  <scm>
    <connection>scm:git:https://github.com/example/project.git</connection>
    <developerConnection>scm:git:ssh://git@github.com/example/project.git</developerConnection>
    <url>https://github.com/example/project/tree/main/site</url>
  </scm>
  ...
  <reporting>
    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-project-info-reports-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${project.version}</version>
        <configuration>
          <webAccessUrl>https://github.com/example/project</webAccessUrl>
          <anonymousConnection>scm:git:https://github.com/example/project.git</anonymousConnection>
          <developerConnection>scm:git:ssh://git@github.com/example/project.git</developerConnection>
        </configuration>
      </plugin>
      ...
    </plugins>
  </reporting>
  ...
</project>
```

<a id="How_to_exclude_SCM_anonymous_access_info"></a>

${esc.h}${esc.h} How to exclude SCM anonymous access info?

Leave out `<connection>` in the `<scm>` element. The report then has no Anonymous Access section:

```xml
<project>
  ...
  <scm>
    <!-- no <connection> -->
    <developerConnection>scm:git:ssh://git@github.com/example/project.git</developerConnection>
    <url>https://github.com/example/project</url>
  </scm>
  ...
</project>
```

**Note:** an empty `<anonymousConnection/>` in the plugin configuration does not remove the section:
Maven treats an empty parameter as unset and falls back to `${esc.d}{project.scm.connection}`.
